
sched/fair: Add optional idle-core wakeup and asym balance checks

Introduce an is_idle_core() helper using available_idle_cpu()
across cpu_smt_mask() to verify that an entire physical core
(all SMT siblings) is idle.

When enabled via sysctl on SMT-active systems:
 - In select_task_rq_fair() on wakeup (WF_TTWU), retain prev_cpu
   if permitted by the task's affinity mask and its entire physical
   core is idle.
 - In asym_active_balance(), require the destination core to be
   completely idle (is_idle_core(env->dst_cpu)) before performing
   an asymmetric active migration.

This preserves L1/L2 cache locality and prevents SMT execution-unit
contention during wakeups and asymmetric packing for latency- and
throughput-sensitive workloads such as gaming, without altering
default EEVDF behavior when disabled.

Runtime control (disabled by default):
   kernel.sched_idlecore_enabled = 0 (default: OFF, mainline EEVDF)
   kernel.sched_idlecore_enabled = 1 (ON, prefer idle physical cores)

