+sched_idlecore_enabled
+======================
+
+Enables idle-core wakeup retention and asymmetric active-balance checks on
+SMT-capable systems.
+
+When enabled (1) and SMT is active, the scheduler:
+
+- Retains ``prev_cpu`` on task wakeup (``WF_TTWU``) if it is allowed by the
+  task's CPU affinity mask and all SMT siblings on its physical core are
+  currently idle.
+- Requires all SMT siblings on the destination physical core to be idle
+  before performing asymmetric active load balancing.
+
+This preserves L1/L2 cache locality and avoids SMT execution-unit contention
+for latency- and throughput-sensitive workloads such as gaming.
+
+0: Disabled (default, standard EEVDF behavior).
+
+1: Enabled.
+
